noetherNormalization -- data for Noether normalization
******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (f,J,X) = noetherNormalization C
  * Inputs:
      * C, which is either an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal, I, or a *note
        quotient ring: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing, R/I where R is a *note
        polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * LimitList => a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, default value {5, 20,
        40, 60, 80, infinity}, gives the value which *note BasisElementLimit:
        (Macaulay2Doc)BasisElementLimit, will take.
      * RandomRange => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 0, if
        not 0, gives a integer bound for the random coefficients. If 0, then
        chooses random elements from the coefficient field.
      * Verbose => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * f, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, an automorphism of R
      * J, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the image of I under f
      * X, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of variables which are
        algebraically independent in R/J

